        <p>PITTS'S Fri. - R N N G ESTABLISHMENT, LONDON-ROAD (cOntinuation of Piccadilly) MANCHESTER. Just put Station, through South Junction Railway Arch.</p>
        <p>PITTS'S announce Stocktaking to have been satisfactory beyond their fondest anticipations. Pitts's turnover during the past 12 months has increased by leaps and bounds and has exceeded that of any previous year by thousands of pounds. Pitts's strain every nerve to give each and every customer the utmost possible satisfaction ; and it is quite evident the public is fully alive to this fact, to judge from the startling increase In Pitts's business.Pitts's are constantly receiving congratulatory letters on their thorough and sys- tematic method of executing orders,which is, the writers say, in marked contrast to orhat Is in vogue at rival establish- ments. Pitts's will ever use their best endeavours to supply good sound articles at moderate prices, as Pitts's are confident that this is the only royal road to success.</p>
        <p>pITTS'S, ever on the alert, have secured, at merely nominal prices, some really magnificent Furniture, Pianos, Pictures, de. frorn the following far.. mansions t•Auburn House, "14roadlands" and "Dmigside. outhport; " "Burlington Howie." Matielb•ster ; "Gin Didsbury; Sr attar," "Stamford Rouse," Ashton ; nose Lea," Sale, dc., do. To give an idea of th-- exceptionally high-class character of these goo's. it may be fretted that the sale at "Auburn House" alone te.slised several thousand pounds. Now Pitts's Intend to promptly cn ar out the-e PXLRAORIMNAEY BAH- (IA I NS. giving their customers the benefit ; so everyone desirous of beautifying their homes at a trifling cost with fur- nishings or a superlative excellence Should visit Pitts's when they will certainly be delighted with the result. Pities will be very pleased indeed to show you round their vast estab- lishment, whether buying or not. Hoods bought and not re- q fred Immediately can be warehoused any reasonable time and insured against fire free of charge. Cash prices only quoted, but deferred payment may be arranged.</p>
        <p>PITTS'S IittAMPLIC DARGIAIN3 —Dining-room Suite, handsomest In Manchester, upholstered throughout with curled hair (guaranteed). small chairs, padded backs, magnificent sideboard fitted with bevelled glasses throughout, brackets, shelves, cupboards, cellarettes. !cc. ; extending table, with patent screw ; overmantel, carnet. brass fender and brass.. ; originally cost £l3O ; Pittes price 62 guineas. Drawhig-room Suite, Chippendale style, solid rosewood, beautifully inlaid with marqueterle work, upholstered throughout with Curled hair (guaranteed), and covered in rich Genoa velvet; magnitleent cabinet and overmantel, occasional. wine, and card tables, all inlaid to match ; carpet, rug, brass fender and brasses, clock and ornaments. com- plete ; cost £173; ritts's price 60 guineas. Bedroom Suite, solid throughout, consists of a very large wardrebe. with bevelled glass doors, drawers, cupboards, Peo. ; pair of large toilet tables, fitted with every convenience ; pedestal towel rail, and chairs complete; a superb suite ; originally cost £B5 : Pitts's price 35 guineas. Hundreds of other bargains on view, equally good value.</p>
        <p>EIMITTS'S HON ti Or FURNITURS. at 14, 22i, 28i. 32i, ..1. 60 up to 1,E0) guineas are renowned far and wide and are honestly worth double the price asked. Fun particulars, press opinions and testimonials on application.</p>
