        <head>BEAR THIS IN MIND.</head>
        <p>BEAR THIS IN MIND.</p>
        <p>A " Cold "is not necessarily the result 'of a high or low temperature. A person may go directly from a hot bath directly into a cold cne, or into snow even,and not take cold. He may remain out in the coldest atmos- phere until chilled through, and still not take cold. On the contary,he may take cold by pouring a couple of teaspoonfuls of water upon some part of his dress, or by standing in a door or before the stove, or by sitting near a window or other opening, when, one part of the body ie colder than the other part. Let it be kept in mind that uniferrnity of temperature over the whole body is the great thing to be looked after. It is the unequal heat upon different parts of the body that produces Colds by disturbing uniform circulation of the bloixl, which in turn induces congestion of some part. Keep the feet always dry and warm, avoid draughts of air, keep the system braced up by plenty of sleep and good food and by a powerful Tonic, and you will be proof against a Cold and its results. The very best Medicine either for preventing or curing a Cold, is</p>
