        <head>-- Dyspeptics and Consumptives should use THE NEW ARTIFICIALLY DIGETED FOOD. PACKARD'S LACTEOLL.</head>
        <p>-- Dyspeptics and Consumptives should use THE NEW ARTIFICIALLY DIGETED FOOD. PACKARD'S LACTEOLL.</p>
        <p>The thinning and wasting in consemption are the most significant signs of this disease F The rapidity with which the body wastes away when an emaciating disease is present lea dansferout symptom. which may not be disregarded with impunity,otherwise the patient drifts to the tom!). . .</p>
        <p>Tido waste can be cheokedior at least retardad,and in many instances the waste of loss can be replaced by ac- tual gain in flesh and weight,by the use of the new arti- ficially digested food Lacteola. The question of diet is all-important in consamption, in all wasting disorders, and in all cases of non-digestion and noe-assimilation of food. The system in all such casesis palpably deficient In digestive capacity, and the dangerous condition has a tendency when neglected to become worse rather than better.</p>
        <p>Even more, by the use of heavy and indigestible oil*, the digestion may be rendered so tried and, overloaded as to be almost incapable of further effbrt. In point of fact this condition is most markedly preva- lest. It may also spring from the inanity tb,properly divst. food of any kind.</p>
        <p>Or the system may, as frequently happeno,digest food affording but little nutriment and be unable to digest the more valuable assimilative food,, or the diet Itself may be lacking in nourishiue and building up force. Food for consumptives and dyspeptics—there is only a narrow streak between tbe two conditions—must be pre-digested before it is swallowed, that, pending the righting power of the digestive organs themselves, the body may be nourished. Lactaola fulfills this requirement to its fullest extent It has been artificially digested outside thn body in act- ually the earns way that Mature herself would adopt (had she st.fficient power to do it) inside the stomach and intestinee.</p>
        <p>- The nourishment in Lacteola ig therefore available for immediate absorption into the blood, wititth means that it at once conveys strength amd vigour to all parts of the body. A want of digestive power will develop a consumpii tive or astemic tendency that otherwise would never show itself. Lacteola, by reinforcing the digestive powers with artificially-digested fond,. wilt enable the digestive functions to recover their lost power.. . . .</p>
        <p>'The foods in Lacteola are specially chosen for their absorbable and asnimilative properties, hence Lacteola combats the wasting as no other food can do. It is practically all absorhecd into the 131°,14, to build up the natural processes of life. There is, in fact,. hardly any waste, because of the pre-iigestion Lacteola has been subjected to before use. You could,indeed, almost live altogether en Lacteola,. but It is not advisable that you should do so, as the. needs of the body are best satisfied with a varied diet.. So that it is an additional advantage in favour of Lac- teola that it prepares the stomach for other foods. Very soon after using Lacteola—a few days at most-- the appetite returns and there is a natural craving for food. This is owing to the fact that by the rest afforded by the use of Lacteola the digestive organs are recover.- strength, and desire work to do so nourishing the body. And when this natural appetite returns to bless the body, thanks to the use of Lactenta, the power of diges- tion returns with it. So that a. healtfre moat meal may be eaten, and above all, digested. Anil being digested the food will go into the blood to nosnish the body and restore strength and vigour to the various processes of life.</p>
        <p>We have two little bpoks which explain mere, about. Lacteola than we can do in an advertisement,and which affords further proof of its. great value. They are ene titled " The Dinner we Eat,' and " The Comeliness ot Health." We will send both post free upon application,. rackard's Lleteola is put up in bottles price Is. 2s. SM. and 4s. 8.1. It is tor sale by raany chemists and medicine vendors;• if, hovv.iver, an difficulty is experi.. priced in obtaining it, it will be sent post free on reeehoa of postal order or stamps for the amount recoired. Manufactured for A. J. White, Limited, 33, Farringdon. Road, London, E.C.</p>
